# Matches the directory and a symlinked node_modules shared between worktrees.
node_modules
dist/
coverage/
.playwright/
playwright-report/
test-results/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.wrangler/

content-export/
.source-cache/

# Blind prose-evaluation working data (never committed; holdout material stays in Drive)
prose-eval-runs/

# Private Art Desk candidate bytes (exact-hash review; never public GitHub)
art/generated/candidates/art-desk/

# Local agent-run-receipt artifacts (scripts/agent-run-receipt.mjs): per-run
# checkout-identity receipts and logs, never tracked historical evidence.
.agent-receipts/

# Storm Events publisher bytes: 243 MB of NCEI .gz files kept outside the
# repository. artifact-lock.json pins every file by sha256; the compiler reads
# them with --raw-dir.
data/source/storm-events-2000-2024/raw/

# Generated prose-corpus reports that regenerate byte-identically from source.
# Committing them put 3.4 GB of near-duplicate revisions into Git history for
# files `npm run corpus:prose` rebuilds on demand. The small human-readable
# reports beside them stay tracked, and so does every baseline.
docs/prose-inventory/coverage-candidates.json
docs/prose-inventory/prose-inventory.json
docs/prose-inventory/prose-inventory.csv
docs/prose-inventory/review-packet.html
# The coverage report and the README are generated too, and they conflicted on
# essentially every base merge: both are mostly per-file lists that move when
# anybody adds a file under `src/`, so two branches adding a source file
# collide by construction. The guarantee the report carried — a stale report
# fails the build — now lives in the five numbers of the tracked
# `coverage-counts.json`, which conflicts only if two branches change the
# totals.
docs/prose-inventory/coverage-report.md
docs/prose-inventory/README.md
